resources.string:
The author of Ra[skobki] asked for game data to improve the puzzles. Consent is optional and doesn't affect the game.

What is collected:
• opening a puzzle;
• the number of a solved bracket, without the word;
• finishing a puzzle: score, time, number of mistakes and hints;
• a random install number and the app version.

What is not collected: diary entries and everything else in the app, email, name, phone model, the words you type.

Where it goes: to the game's author. The server receiving the data technically sees the phone's IP address.

Opting out: any time in the Ra[skobki] profile. What was collected on the phone and the install number are deleted right away.

Separately from this consent: if you are signed in, progress, answers and results go to the game's server, as on the site. The account doesn't work without this.
